  "tabs": [
    {
      "tabname": "Details",
      "class": "DepictionStackView",
      "views": [
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "Replaces the lock screen clock with images, and lets you install your own digit packs.\n\nBuilt against the CoverSheetKit lock screen, for iOS 18."
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "Features"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "- Animated or still digits\n- Four packs included — Anime, Pixel, CRT and Sakura\n- Installable digit packs, imported and removed from Settings\n- Adjustable animation speed\n- Adjustable digit size, spacing and vertical offset\n- 12-hour, 24-hour or system time format\n- Optional date hiding\n- Colour tinting that keeps the artwork's shading, the way iOS tints app icons\n- Switch to still frames while Low Power Mode is on\n- Settings apply live, no respring needed\n- Falls back to the stock clock if the selected pack is unusable"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "Digit packs"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "A pack is a folder named `<Name>.flexpack` containing an `animated` and/or `static` folder with `0`–`9` and `colon` as GIF or PNG. Animated GIF and APNG both play at their own frame timing. Drop one into `/var/mobile/Library/FlexClock/Packs` or import it from **Settings → FlexClock → Manage packs**."
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
